  "text": "Thank you all — this is very helpful. Let me synthesize what I'm hearing. Jonas, the corrected borrowing base gives us $6,750,000 maximum availability at the 75% advance rate against $9 million in eligible receivables — well below the $12 million requested. Elena, legal requires a first-priority UCC filing and a controlled lockbox as conditions precedent before any drawdown — both non-negotiable. Ravi, the $1,500,000 cash equity contribution before the first draw is a meaningful piece of the funding structure. So combining the borrowing-base availability of $6,750,000 with the $1,500,000 equity contribution, we're looking at roughly $8,250,000 in total funding capacity against the $12 million requested. That's a significant gap. Before I make my decision, I want to confirm with the group: does anyone see a path to closing that gap, or should we be thinking about structuring this as a smaller facility — perhaps at the $6,750,000 borrowing-base limit — with the equity contribution as additional support? I'm also interested in whether the relationship team believes the client would accept revised terms."
}
